## Known nits (carry forward)

None open.

Addressed 2026-08-22: GLFW refcount is mutex-protected and incremented only
after successful `glfwInit`. `requestClose()` is no longer `const`. The
`// TODO(jade):` tag format is in active use (grep confirms) — the 2026-08-19
nit about it is resolved. A later hygiene pass added: 4.1 fallback rung,
context save/restore + exception barriers in GLFW callbacks, sticky input +
auto-tracked edge queries, Shader uniform location cache with warn-once and
bind-before-set, Logger stdout flush on errors, `GLFW_INCLUDE_NONE`, and a
catch-all in `main`.

